/**
@page targets Targets

@brief Building and running each build target, and porting to new hardware.

`libbotanik` builds for two targets from one codebase, both running the same site
verbatim - the only difference is who owns the PLC shared memory.

- @subpage md_src_2botanik__sim_2README - the Linux simulator (`SIMULATOR`): runs on
  the host; the harness allocates the shared region locally and drives a mock PLC.
- @subpage md_src_2botanik__fw_2README - the Arduino OPTA firmware (`OPTA`):
  cross-compiled for the STM32H747, shipped as an Arduino library zip; the real M4
  coprocessor owns the shared region.
- @subpage porting - what a third target needs: a new HAL implementation behind the
  same interface.
*/
